<title>BRAZIL: Soy shipping conditions at Brazil's Santos port.</title>
<headline>Soy shipping conditions at Brazil's Santos port.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santos port reported the following conditions for shipments of soybeans and soymeal:</p>
<p>Vessels: Tomis Future continues loading 50,000 tonnes soybeans, expected to leave March 18. Ziemia Krakowska waiting to complete loading 19,000 tonnes soymeal, due to take place of Tomis Future. Ossolineum loading 55,000 tonnes soybeans at Cargill private terminal.</p>
<p>Road: 195 trucks arrived over the weekend unloading 5,134 tonnes soybeans.</p>
<p>Rail: 40 wagons arrived, unloading 1,906 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Stocks: 73,041 tonnes soybeans, 8,772 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
</text>
